# Appearance & theming

Appearance is OS-wide and owned by `useTheme` + `src/lib/appearance.ts`. Persist in `martijnos-theme` localStorage. Apply with `applyAppearance()` (sets `html` class/data attrs + CSS vars).

## Controls (Settings → Appearance)

- **Mode:** `light` | `dark` | `auto` → toggles `.dark` (auto follows `prefers-color-scheme`)
- **Liquid Glass:** `clear` | `tinted` → `--glass-blur`, `--glass-saturate`, chrome alphas (`--menubar-bg`, `--sidebar`, `--dock-bg`, `--window-body`, `--settings-*`)
- **Accent colour:** `--macos-accent`, also `--ring` / `--sidebar-primary`
- **Text highlight:** `--macos-highlight` + `::selection`
- Also: icon style, folder colour, sidebar icon size, wallpaper window tint, scroll bars

## Rules

- Never hardcode `#007aff` / `#0a84ff` for interactive chrome — use `var(--macos-accent)` or Tailwind `bg-[var(--macos-accent)]`
- Glass surfaces use `blur(var(--glass-blur)) saturate(var(--glass-saturate))` and token backgrounds, not fixed rgba
- Shadcn controls should look macOS: prefer `.macos-input`, `.macos-select`, `.macos-button`, `Switch`, `RadioGroup` from `src/components/ui/`
- New OS chrome (dock, menubar, titlebar, sidebars) must read appearance tokens so Settings changes apply immediately
- Do not invent a second theme store; extend `ThemeConfig` in `appearance.ts` + `useTheme`
